Derivative work
---------------
  omp-claude-bridge
  Copyright (c) 2026 Jonathan Borgwing (https://github.com/DevVig)
  Licensed under the MIT License.

  Changes from the original:
    - Ported the extension from Pi (@earendil-works/*) to Oh My Pi
      (@oh-my-pi/*), including the extension manifest, provider registration,
      message conversion, and config directory resolution.
    - Added a `provider.contextWindow` setting ("auto" | "1m" | "200k") that
      forces the Claude Code context window across every model, hiding models
      that have no runtime for the selected window.

Second derivative work
-----------------------
  omp-claude-bridge (this fork)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Yuri Vidal (https://github.com/esp3tek)
  Licensed under the MIT License.

  Changes from DevVig/omp-claude-bridge 0.8.1:
    - Session sync: a main-thread context shorter than the session cursor
      rebuilds instead of starting clean, so a turn can no longer run with no
      history at all; reentrant (subagent) calls never rebuild or adopt the
      shared session.
    - Forwards omp's own system prompt and the full text of tool descriptions
      Claude Code truncates at 2048 characters, with an optional host-only
      prompt mode; isolates the child from ~/.claude settings.
    - Serves omp's JSON schemas to Claude Code verbatim and pairs tool results
      by Claude Code's tool_use id (ported from pi-claude-bridge).
    - Mid-turn steering through a parked stdin generator (ported from
      pi-claude-bridge 0.7.0), replacing the deferred-replay loop.
    - Pre-warms the next Claude Code process between turns.
    - Reports Claude subscription quota (5h / 7d windows) to omp.
    - Builds the model list from Claude Code's own picker, with a static
      fallback; adds Claude Fable 5.1 and Opus 5.
    - Leaves compaction summaries to omp instead of taking them over inside an
      extension handler the host aborts at 30 seconds.
    - Re-registers the provider after a finished subagent tears down the
      extension source's runtime providers.
    - Surfaces an exhausted subscription as a 429 so omp walks its fallback
      chain, and names safeguard refusals instead of retrying them blindly.

